hint.txt:
    A C command-line program (C11), built with CMake (3.14 or later), with unit tests in GoogleTest (C++).
    - Layout: put the program's logic in a small C library inside the project, and keep main.c thin, so the GoogleTest tests can call the C functions directly (with extern "C" where needed). Use {{NAME_SNAKE}} for C identifiers, such as function prefixes, header names and include guards, and {{NAME}} for the executable and the CMake project.
    - GoogleTest: when find_package(GTest) finds an installed copy, build the tests and register them with CTest. Download it with FetchContent only when the developer opts in, with a CMake option that is off by default. With neither, configure and build the program anyway and skip the tests, with a message.
    - tests/smoke.sh: configure and build in a temporary build folder (never in the source tree), run the program, and check its placeholder line, --help and --version. Run ctest only when GoogleTest was found, and say when the tests were skipped. Never download anything. Work with Apple clang on macOS and with gcc on Linux.
    - README: building, running, testing, and how to get GoogleTest (Homebrew, apt, or the opt-in download).

